[dump]{"page":10,"cssW":612,"cssH":792,"blocks":[{"cls":"plain text","rect":[49.7,468,287.1,574.6],"paras":[{"t":"As a general framework, Mask R-CNN is compat- ible with complementary techniques developed for de- tection/segmentation, including improvements made to Fast/Faster R-CNN and FCNs. In this appendix we de- scribe some techniques that improve over our original re- sults. Thanks to its generality and flexibility, Mask R-CNN was used as the framework by the three winning teams in the COCO 2017 instance segmentation competition, which all significantly outperformed the previous state of the art.","ls":[{"x":62.1,"t":"As a general framework, Mask R-CNN is compat-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"ible with complementary techniques developed for de-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"tection/segmentation, including improvements made to"},{"x":50.1,"t":"Fast/Faster R-CNN and FCNs. In this appendix we de-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"scribe some techniques that improve over our original re-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"sults. Thanks to its generality and flexibility, Mask R-CNN"},{"x":50.1,"t":"was used as the framework by the three winning teams in"},{"x":50.1,"t":"the COCO 2017 instance segmentation competition, which"},{"x":50.1,"t":"all significantly outperformed the previous state of the art."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[49.6,319.7,287.6,438.8],"paras":[{"t":"We report some enhanced results of Mask R-CNN in Ta- ble 8. Overall, the improvements increase mask AP 5.1 points (from 36.7 to 41.8) and box AP 7.7 points (from 39.6 to 47.3). Each model improvement increases both mask AP and box AP consistently, showing good generalization of the Mask R-CNN framework. We detail the improvements next. These results, along with future updates, can be repro- duced by our released code at https://github.com/ facebookresearch/Detectron, and can serve as higher baselines for future research.","ls":[{"x":62.1,"t":"We report some enhanced results of Mask R-CNN in Ta-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"ble 8. Overall, the improvements increase mask AP 5.1"},{"x":50.1,"t":"points (from 36.7 to 41.8) and box AP 7.7 points (from 39.6"},{"x":50.1,"t":"to 47.3). Each model improvement increases both mask AP"},{"x":50.1,"t":"and box AP consistently, showing good generalization of"},{"x":50.1,"t":"the Mask R-CNN framework. We detail the improvements"},{"x":50.1,"t":"next. These results, along with future updates, can be repro-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"duced by our released code at https://github.com/"},{"x":50.1,"t":"facebookresearch/Detectron, and can serve as"},{"x":50.1,"t":"higher baselines for future research."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308.2,525.8,546,597],"paras":[{"t":"Train-time augmentation: Scale augmentation at train time further improves results. During training, we randomly sample a scale from [640, 800] pixels and we increase the number of iterations to 260k (with the learning rate reduced by 10 at 200k and 240k iterations). Train-time augmenta- tion improves mask AP by 0.6 and box AP by 0.8.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"Train-time augmentation: Scale augmentation at train"},{"x":308.9,"t":"time further improves results. During training, we randomly"},{"x":308.9,"t":"sample a scale from [640, 800] pixels and we increase the"},{"x":308.9,"t":"number of iterations to 260k (with the learning rate reduced"},{"x":308.9,"t":"by 10 at 200k and 240k iterations). Train-time augmenta-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"tion improves mask AP by 0.6 and box AP by 0.8."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[49.7,150.8,287.2,245.5],"paras":[{"t":"End-to-end training: All previous results used stage- wise training, i.e., training RPN as the first stage and Mask R-CNN as the second. Following [37], we evaluate end- to-end (‘e2e’) training that jointly trains RPN and Mask R- CNN. We adopt the ‘approximate’ version in [37] that only computes partial gradients in the RoIAlign layer by ignor- ing the gradient w.r.t. RoI coordinates. Table 8 shows that e2e training improves mask AP by 0.6 and box AP by 1.2.","ls":[{"x":62.1,"t":"End-to-end training: All previous results used stage-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"wise training, i.e., training RPN as the first stage and Mask"},{"x":50.1,"t":"R-CNN as the second. Following [37], we evaluate end-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"to-end (‘e2e’) training that jointly trains RPN and Mask R-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"CNN. We adopt the ‘approximate’ version in [37] that only"},{"x":50.1,"t":"computes partial gradients in the RoIAlign layer by ignor-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"ing the gradient w.r.t. RoI coordinates. Table 8 shows that"},{"x":50.1,"t":"e2e training improves mask AP by 0.6 and box AP by 1.2."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[49.6,247.6,287.3,317.9],"paras":[{"t":"Updated baseline: We start with an updated baseline with a different set of hyper-parameters. We lengthen the training to 180k iterations, in which the learning rate is re- duced by 10 at 120k and 160k iterations. We also change the NMS threshold to 0.5 (from a default value of 0.3). The updated baseline has 37.0 mask AP and 40.5 box AP.","ls":[{"x":62.1,"t":"Updated baseline: We start with an updated baseline"},{"x":50.1,"t":"with a different set of hyper-parameters. We lengthen the"},{"x":50.1,"t":"training to 180k iterations, in which the learning rate is re-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"duced by 10 at 120k and 160k iterations. We also change"},{"x":50.1,"t":"the NMS threshold to 0.5 (from a default value of 0.3). The"},{"x":50.1,"t":"updated baseline has 37.0 mask AP and 40.5 box AP."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[49.7,78.4,287,149.5],"paras":[{"t":"ImageNet-5k pre-training: Following [45], we experi- ment with models pre-trained on a 5k-class subset of Ima- geNet (in contrast to the standard 1k-class subset). This 5× increase in pre-training data improves both mask and box 1 AP. As a reference, [40] used ∼250× more images (300M) and reported a 2-3 box AP improvement on their baselines.","ls":[{"x":62.1,"t":"ImageNet-5k pre-training: Following [45], we experi-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"ment with models pre-trained on a 5k-class subset of Ima-"},{"x":50.1,"t":"geNet (in contrast to the standard 1k-class subset). This 5×"},{"x":50.1,"t":"increase in pre-training data improves both mask and box 1"},{"x":50.1,"t":"AP. As a reference, [40] used 250× more images (300M)"},{"x":50.1,"t":"and reported a 2-3 box AP improvement on their baselines."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308.1,102.7,545.9,221.6],"paras":[{"t":"With a recent method called data distillation [35], we are able to exploit the additional 120k unlabeled images pro- vided by COCO. In brief, data distillation is a self-training strategy that uses a model trained on labeled data to pre- dict annotations on unlabeled images, and in turn updates the model with these new annotations. Mask R-CNN pro- vides an effective framework for such a self-training strat- egy. With data distillation, Mask R-CNN APkp improve by 1.8 points to 69.1. We observe that Mask R-CNN can ben- efit from extra data, even if that data is unlabeled.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"With a recent method called data distillation [35], we are"},{"x":308.9,"t":"able to exploit the additional 120k unlabeled images pro-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"vided by COCO. In brief, data distillation is a self-training"},{"x":308.9,"t":"strategy that uses a model trained on labeled data to pre-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"dict annotations on unlabeled images, and in turn updates"},{"x":308.9,"t":"the model with these new annotations. Mask R-CNN pro-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"vides an effective framework for such a self-training strat-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"egy. With data distillation, Mask R-CNN AP improve by"},{"x":308.9,"t":"1.8 points to 69.1. We observe that Mask R-CNN can ben-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"efit from extra data, even if that data is unlabeled."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308.3,321.8,546.2,380.6],"paras":[{"t":"The above result is the foundation of our submission to the COCO 2017 competition (which also used an ensemble, not discussed here). The first three winning teams for the instance segmentation task were all reportedly based on an extension of the Mask R-CNN framework.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"The above result is the foundation of our submission to"},{"x":308.9,"t":"the COCO 2017 competition (which also used an ensemble,"},{"x":308.9,"t":"not discussed here). The first three winning teams for the"},{"x":308.9,"t":"instance segmentation task were all reportedly based on an"},{"x":308.9,"t":"extension of the Mask R-CNN framework."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308.3,429.6,546.3,476.4],"paras":[{"t":"Using the recently proposed non-local (NL) model [43], we achieve 40.3 mask AP and 45.0 box AP. This result is without test-time augmentation, and the method runs at 3fps on an Nvidia Tesla P100 GPU at test time.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"Using the recently proposed non-local (NL) model [43],"},{"x":308.9,"t":"we achieve 40.3 mask AP and 45.0 box AP. This result is"},{"x":308.9,"t":"without test-time augmentation, and the method runs at 3fps"},{"x":308.9,"t":"on an Nvidia Tesla P100 GPU at test time."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308.5,381.8,546,428.4],"paras":[{"t":"Test-time augmentation: We combine the model results evaluated using scales of [400, 1200] pixels with a step of 100 and on their horizontal flips. This gives us a single- model result of 41.8 mask AP and 47.3 box AP.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"Test-time augmentation: We combine the model results"},{"x":308.9,"t":"evaluated using scales of [400, 1200] pixels with a step of"},{"x":308.9,"t":"100 and on their horizontal flips. This gives us a single-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"model result of 41.8 mask AP and 47.3 box AP."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308.4,477.9,546.2,524.5],"paras":[{"t":"Model architecture: By upgrading the 101-layer ResNeXt to its 152-layer counterpart [19], we observe an increase of 0.5 mask AP and 0.6 box AP. This shows a deeper model can still improve results on COCO.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"Model architecture: By upgrading the 101-layer"},{"x":308.9,"t":"ResNeXt to its 152-layer counterpart [19], we observe an"},{"x":308.9,"t":"increase of 0.5 mask AP and 0.6 box AP. This shows a"},{"x":308.9,"t":"deeper model can still improve results on COCO."}]}]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308.2,222.8,545.8,293.6],"paras":[{"t":"We report enhanced results of keypoint detection in Ta- ble 9. As an updated baseline, we extend the training sched- ule to 130k iterations in which the learning rate is reduced by 10 at 100k and 120k iterations. This improves APkp by about 1 point. Replacing ResNet-50 with ResNet-101 and ResNeXt-101 increases APkp to 66.1 and 67.3, respectively.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"We report enhanced results of keypoint detection in Ta-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"ble 9. As an updated baseline, we extend the training sched-"},{"x":308.9,"t":"ule to 130k iterations in which the learning rate is reduced"},{"x":308.9,"t":"by 10 at 100k and 120k iterations. This improves AP by"},{"x":308.9,"t":"about 1 point. Replacing ResNet-50 with ResNet-101 and"},{"x":308.9,"t":"ResNeXt-101 increases AP to 66.1 and 67.3, respectively."}]}]},{"cls":"table","rect":[51.4,642.4,286.9,721.7],"paras":[]},{"cls":"table","rect":[309.8,654.9,546.3,721.7],"paras":[]},{"cls":"plain text","rect":[308,78.6,545.8,101.4],"paras":[{"t":"By using the same test-time augmentation as used for instance segmentation, we further boost APkp to 70.4.","ls":[{"x":320.8,"t":"By using the same test-time augmentation as used for"},{"x":308.9,"t":"instance segmentation, we further boost AP to 70.4."}]}]},{"cls":"title","rect":[49.7,445.7,258.8,458.1],"paras":[{"t":"Instance Segmentation and Object Detection","ls":[{"x":50.1,"t":"Instance Segmentation and Object Detection"}]}]},{"cls":"title","rect":[49.6,583.1,264.3,596.8],"paras":[{"t":"Appendix B: Enhanced Results on COCO","ls":[{"x":50.1,"t":"Appendix B: Enhanced Results on COCO"}]}]},{"cls":"title","rect":[308.6,300.2,399.3,312.5],"paras":[{"t":"Keypoint Detection","ls":[{"x":308.9,"t":"Keypoint Detection"}]}]},{"cls":"abandon","rect":[292.8,49.9,303.2,58.7],"paras":[]},{"cls":"table_